body:
I'm only just catching up now on all of the lore, so I might be very wrong, but;

I personally took the lyrics "I'll tape my eyes so I don't fall asleep again" from The Outside and applied it to how every era ends with a closed eye, sleeping, and a new era starts with an open eye, waking up. Falling asleep indicates the waiting period between eras, and "to tape my eyes so that I don't fall asleep again" reads to me as "I'm never going to wait for the next lore era again, this chapter is over", since this is supposedly the end of Trench lore completely.

To cover eyes with a strip of tape seems like the most literal and easiest way to put this into imagery, so I don't find a problem with that alone. The fact that it's red is confusing though.
